Hi.

I get two dmesg messages that request me to test some things and mail
them. The first one is:

[    0.000000] ACPI: BIOS bug: multiple APIC/MADT found, using 0
[    0.000000] ACPI: If "acpi_apic_instance=3D2" works better, notify
linux-acpi@vger.kernel.org

I've tried booting with acpi_apic_instance=3D2, but since I don't have any
idea what difference it should make I can only tell you that both boot
without any problems. Of course 0 and 2 switch places in the message
above.

The second one is this:

[   45.085604] ACPI: System BIOS is requesting _OSI(Linux)
[   45.085609] ACPI: Please test with "acpi_osi=3D!Linux"
[   45.085612] Please send dmidecode to linux-acpi@vger.kernel.org

I've attached the output of dmidecode. It doesn't change with the
parameter acpi_osi=3D!Linux added. Actually, nothing does - even the dmsg
message remains unchanged. I even double checked that GRUB actually
passed the parameter to the kernel, and it does.

Hope this helps.
